  "id": "COMPOUND:22910 - PROTEIN:2270",
  "verbalization": "Pentylbenzene is implicated in the target relationship with mRNA interferase EndoA through a series of indirect pathways, all leading to the Type-2 angiotensin II receptor. This receptor is the common target of multiple compounds, including Alsterpaullone and 1-Tridecene-3,5,7,9,11-pentayne, which in turn have a shared target of EndoA. The evidence suggests that Pentylbenzene may act as a modulator or activator of the Type-2 angiotensin II receptor, which then serves as a bridge to EndoA. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target relationships implies a potential mechanism of action involving receptor activation or signaling pathways that ultimately lead to EndoA engagement. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Pentylbenzene in influencing the activity of EndoA through a receptor-mediated mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
